Requirement:
Coin Operated Pay Phone — Polished Requirement Specification

Functional Requirements
1. The system shall start when it is not in use.
2. The system shall require inserting coins when the user picks up the receiver.
3. The system shall allow dialing a number only after sufficient credit has been added.
4. The system shall start the call when the dialed number is valid and the other party answers.
5. The system shall continue the call as long as there is sufficient credit.
6. The system shall end the call if the credit runs out during the call.
7. The system shall allow adding more coins to continue the call.
8. The system shall return any unused coins when the user hangs up.
9. The system shall return to an unused state after a call ends.

Invalid PlantUML:
@startuml
title Coin Operated Pay Phone State Machine

[*] --> Idle

Idle --> Active : lift receiver / get dial tone
Active --> DialTone : lift receiver / get dial tone
DialTone --> CreditCheck : enter coins
CreditCheck --> CallStart : valid number dialed and answered
CallStart --> Calling : call in progress
Calling --> CreditCheck : check credit during call
Calling --> EndCall : credit runs out
EndCall --> Idle : hang up

state Idle {
    [*] --> Active : lift receiver / get dial tone
}

state Active {
    [*] --> DialTone : lift receiver / get dial tone
}

state DialTone {
    [*] --> CreditCheck : enter coins
}

state CreditCheck {
    [*] --> CallStart : valid number dialed and answered
}

state CallStart {
    [*] --> Calling : call in progress
}

state Calling {
    [*] --> CreditCheck : check credit during call
    [*] --> EndCall : credit runs out
}

state EndCall {
    [*] --> Idle : hang up
}
@enduml

Validation Errors:
- multiple_initial_state_transitions
- missing_final_state_transition

Relevant Rule:
- multiple_initial_state_transitions: A valid state diagram should have one clear top-level initial transition. Remove or restructure extra top-level [*] transitions.
- missing_final_state_transition: A valid state diagram must include at least one final transition from a natural terminal state to [*].

